Permitted Use

Use of the Software is permitted free of charge for any purpose, including
internal commercial use, by any person or organization, such as companies,
pharmaceutical companies, biotechnology companies, academic institutions,
nonprofits, and other entities. This explicitly includes asset development, drug
discovery, the design and reworking of binders and other molecules, modification
of the Software, the creation of derivative works, and the redistribution of
source code or binaries for others to run themselves, whether for academic or
commercial purposes and whether free of charge or for a fee.

Permitted use includes running the Software locally, on private infrastructure,
in a private cloud environment, or on infrastructure managed for the sole
benefit of the using organization, as well as providing the design outputs of
the Software (for example designed binders, sequences, or structures) to others
as a result or service.

"Third Parties" means persons or entities other than you, your affiliates, and
your employees or contractors using the Software on your behalf for your
internal purposes.

Hosted Service Restriction

You may not, without a separate written commercial license from the copyright
holders, provide the Software, a modified version of the Software, or a service
whose material functionality is provided by or derived from the Software, to
Third Parties as a hosted, managed, cloud, API, web application, workflow
platform, or software-as-a-service offering, where that offering provides Third
Parties with access to any substantial set of the features or functionality of
the Software (a "Hosted Service").

The distribution of a substantially preconfigured deployment of the Software
(for example a container, virtual machine image, or installer) that is intended
to be operated as a Hosted Service by the recipient is treated as provision of a
Hosted Service for the purposes of this section, where the purpose or effect is
to circumvent it.

Making the Software available to Third Parties as an invocable tool, plugin,
agent action, connector, or workflow step within a hosted platform, such that
those Third Parties can run the functionality of the Software without installing
it themselves, is treated as provision of a Hosted Service for the purposes of
this section. For clarity, this does not apply where a Third Party has installed
the Software themselves, or on infrastructure operated for their sole benefit,
and directs its execution through their own agent, script, or automated tooling.

For clarity, the redistribution of source code or binaries for others to run
themselves, the internal use of the Software (including execution directed by
your own automated or agentic tooling), and the provision of design outputs (for
example designed binders, sequences, or structures) are not Hosted Services and
require no commercial license.

